  {
   "start_phrase": "Start in Settings",
   "line": "Start in Settings, because that's where the phone tells you what it's doing: open it and look just above General, near the top of the list. If you see a row called Optimising Search and Siri, your phone is still working through the update in the background. That work is what's using your battery. You can't switch it off from here, because it's a status rather than a setting, but it tells you exactly what you're dealing with.",
