  {
   "start_phrase": "While you wait",
   "line": "While you wait, there's one habit worth dropping, because a lot of people swipe every app out of the app switcher to save battery and it doesn't help at all. In 2017 a customer emailed Apple's software chief to ask whether he force quits apps, and whether doing it preserves battery life. His reply, published by Daring Fireball, was two words: no and no. I stopped doing it years ago for exactly that reason. Your iPhone already freezes the apps you aren't using, so closing them just means loading them again from scratch later, which uses more power.",
   "mark": "GFX",
   "cut": "core",
   "tier": "official",
