  {
   "start_phrase": "If a few days have passed",
   "line": "If a few days have passed and the drain hasn't eased, check your battery's health next. Open Settings, tap Battery, then Battery Health, and look at Maximum Capacity. That number is counted in full charge cycles. Apple rates an iPhone 14 or earlier to keep eighty percent of its capacity after five hundred of them, and an iPhone 15 or later after a thousand, so one heavy week of indexing can't move it. If the capacity looks normal and the update note has gone, that's when it's worth taking the phone to Apple.",
